     "result_text_tail": "n (32%).\n\n**Choices I made without you**\n- **Theme:** navy. **Audience:** CEO and board deciding at the March 2027 meeting.\n- **$40M ambition:** read as a 2030 target. The deck says plainly that no route reaches it, and the next steps ask the board to restate its date.\n- **Cash method:** inventory is four months of landed cost, counted as a cash outflow as it builds up. One-time costs (fixtures, launch fee, setup) are treated as expenses. Doors count for a full year. Group margin is measured against the ex-US plan, and 2027 is the lowest year for every option.\n- **Japan scale-up:** excludes working capital, because the pack doesn't give it.\n- **Advertising sensitivity:** the deck shows the plan's 25% and the agency's 32%. The pilot's 28% appears as text next to the 28.6% break-even.\n\n**Numbers:** 194 in total, all traced to the briefing pack. 106 come straight from it; 88 are calculations from those, each with its formula. Five are marked as estimates (the no-halo and tariff cases), with their basis shown on the slide. No placeholders are left. I didn't run the web-source re-check, since there are no web sources.\n\nTo change a number or a slide, edit `work/build_spec.py`, which rebuilds the spec. Next I could switch the theme or add a backup slide with the realistic case for the retail route at 2.6 units per door.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx (one sheet per slide, plus calculations)\n- onsoo-us-entry.json (the storyline spec)"
